diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ec26ccb..3ddff5c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -22,6 +22,12 @@ The single-process Puma deployment uses Action Cable for phase-change notificati
 
 Moderator transitions and answer writes check the expected phase and round under a database lock. Delayed submissions cannot reopen a question or land in a later round. If deploying multiple Puma processes in the future, use a shared Action Cable adapter for cross-process notifications.
 
+## Question timer
+
+Set **Timer minutes** and **Timer seconds** in quiz settings. Both default to zero (manual finish only). A game snapshots the duration and measures each countdown from the stored question opening time. Only the moderator sees the countdown and can finish early. Timer settings are not exported.
+
+An in-process job closes each timed question using the same guarded transition as **Finish**. Screen reads and answer submissions also check the deadline, so a server restart cannot extend a question.
+
 ## Scoring and prizes
 
 Games also snapshot **Number of winners** (default 3). Each accepted pick replaces both the previous choice and its server-measured elapsed time since the round opened. Ending a game freezes its leaderboard: most correct answers first, then least total time on correct answers, then join order for an exact tie.
